## Exploratory failures and limits

Initial fixture attempts lacked the junction's side-card identifiers and then
used an inconsistent anchor spelling. Those were fixture errors, corrected
before recording the three baseline behavioral failures above.

An extra exploratory all-set case attempted to include an abstract module
before that module's Ruby-compatible load phase. It correctly failed with
`UnknownSetIncludeTargetError`, including when the files were split across
mods because pattern groups are the outer load loop. Its initial actual
95-test/one-failure output is preserved in
`cross-pattern-format-ancestry-2026-10-30.fixture-check.tests.json`. The invalid
extra fixture and speculative all-set ordering change were removed. The final
94-test result is the distinct run described above.

An initial typecheck log is retained as the empty
`cross-pattern-format-ancestry-2026-10-30.typecheck.txt`. A protection check
refused overwriting that existing leased file; it was preserved. The final
typecheck ran without replacing any log and exited zero. No gate was changed.

